6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.200
Let's dive in.

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.800
You understand that there are vast
amount of data on the internet right now,

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.900
and there are few ways
to compare the similarity

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.900
or how closely one data point
is to another.

10
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.700
A common method is text search,
where you match

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.900
a query keyword with a parts
of the content of a data point

12
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.133
to compute a match.

13
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:39.133
This is information
retrieval at the basic sense,

14
00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:43.533
where you input a keyword or a search
term, match against several data

15
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:46.533
points, and detect
