accommodate, address, summary,

492
00:29:40.700 --> 00:29:43.700
and other specified attributes.

493
00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:46.533
To handle user queries you define

494
00:29:46.533 --> 00:29:49.533
a function called handle user query.

495
00:29:49.533 --> 00:29:52.800
Handle user query function
would take into user query,

496
00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:55.900
the database object, and the collection

497
00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:58.900
object as its argument.

498
00:29:58.933 --> 00:30:02.000
And now you get to use the vector
search function.

499
00:30:03.100 --> 00:30:06.100
Call the vector
search function, pass in the query

500
00:30:06.100 --> 00:30:09.100
the database object
and the collection object,

501
00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:12.533
and assigning the results
to a variable called Get Knowledge.

502
00:30:12.800 --> 00:30:16.500
Get knowledge
will hold the list of the documents

503
00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:19.500
retrieved through the vector
search operation.

504
00:30:19.933 --> 00:30:23.600
You conduct a sanity check
to ensure get knowledge is not empty.

505
00:30:24.033 --> 00:30:27.933
Once you've obtained the search results
from vector

506
00:30:27.933 --> 00:30:31.200
search operation
held in the get knowledge variable,

507
00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:35.500
you will convert them and ensure

508
00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:38.600
they meet the specified model

509
00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:41.633
defined in the search result item.

510
00:30:41.633 --> 00:30:44.633
The next step is to convert
the search results

511
00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:48.100
into data frames.

512
00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:51.900
This allows for efficient modification
of the search results.

513
00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:54.533
In this step

514
00:30:54.533 --> 00:30:57.800
you will pause the query
and the search results

515
00:30:58.100 --> 00:31:01.100
to the LLM.

516
00:31:01.133 --> 00:31:04.500
In this course, you were using GPT-3.5

517
00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:08.133
turbo as the LLM for the RAG system.

518
00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:12.600
Here you are specifying to the system
that it's an Airbnb

519
00:31:12.600 --> 00:31:15.700
listing recommendation system
and passing in the query

520
00:31:16.100 --> 00:31:20.900
along with additional context
held in the search results.

521
00:31:20.900 --> 00:31:23.600
Data frame variable.

522
00:31:23.600 --> 00:31:26.600
The following step extracts

523
00:31:26.933 --> 00:31:30.000
the response from the LLM.

524
00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:31.600
You extract the response

525
00:31:31.600 --> 00:31:35.233
