528
00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:46.633
and observation into the process
occurring.

529
00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:51.133
The final step here is to display
the search result as a table,

530
00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:56.300
which holds the additional context
passed into the LLM as input.

531
00:31:57.400 --> 00:32:02.333
The handle user query function will return
the system response.

532
00:32:02.900 --> 00:32:07.600
This is the final step for this lesson
where you assign a string,

533
00:32:08.100 --> 00:32:10.600
representing a query
to a variable called query,

534
00:32:11.533 --> 00:32:14.533
and pass
the query into the handle user function

535
00:32:14.800 --> 00:32:17.800
along with the database and collection
object.

536
00:32:17.900 --> 00:32:22.900
The query you are using for this lesson
and course is specifically

537
00:32:23.633 --> 00:32:28.633
one that indicates to the system
to recommend an Airbnb listing

538
00:32:28.833 --> 00:32:32.600
